1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:02,030
Tonight, you might dream you're running,

2
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,850
while your body lies almost perfectly still.

3
00:00:04,890 --> 00:00:07,830
In REM sleep, circuits in your brainstem

4
00:00:07,830 --> 00:00:10,500
shut down signals to most of your muscles.

5
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:13,830
This temporary paralysis, called REM atonia,

6
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:16,500
helps stop you from acting out your dreams.

7
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,080
But your eyes keep darting,

8
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,488
and your breathing muscles keep working.

9
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,200
When this system fails,

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,115
some people physically act out their dreams.

11
00:00:26,390 --> 00:00:28,210
So tonight, your brain will keep you still...

12
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:29,000
on purpose.
